Author:     Christie Hubley <christie@tinkerartstudio.com>
AuthorDate: Wed Oct 7 13:24:49 2026 -0600
Commit:     Christie Hubley <christie@tinkerartstudio.com>
CommitDate: Wed Oct 7 13:24:49 2026 -0600

    D-4: a Force run is keyed by the day it actually runs (DECISIONS #64)
    
    V-4's failure-first Force run (Oct 7) showed Cloud Scheduler sends a Force run
    the job's NEXT scheduled time, not now, so a weekday catch-up would take the
    coming Sunday's key and that Sunday's real run would skip as "already done".
    runKey now keys a scheduled time still in the future by today's UTC date; a
    real run and its retries keep their scheduled date. New test fails on the old
    code. Runbook (FUNCTIONS-ROLLBACK.md §10) and DATA-RESTORE.md updated.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

