    11	//      resumed, their prefixes never reused.
    12	//   3. Otherwise export to a fresh prefix weekly/<key>-<6 chars> and wait on it — unless less than START_RESERVE_MS of
    13	//      the budget is left, when it throws instead and the next retry starts it.
    14	// The budget is 1,500 s from the start of the run, and it bounds EVERY call to Google as well as the waiting (each call
    15	// gets only the time that's left, deadline.js), so the error and its alert always happen before Cloud Run's 1,800 s
    16	// kill; the next retry resumes at step 2. Success needs: done, no error, state SUCCESSFUL, the expected prefix, and
    17	// the complete folder visible in the bucket. Anything else throws.
    18	//
    19	// A rare duplicate (two runs racing, or a lost reply not yet listed) is a second COMPLETE copy in its own folder, never
    20	// a mixed one (Christie, O5). State is the bucket plus the operation list; there is no Firestore collection.
